# Named actuals (the book, named-actuals; M6 4a, slice 345): a named actual `zz: 5` names a formal the selected callable
# does not have -- the refusal of the call at translation, before any argument is computed.
fn: tst (int: c 3; int: a 2) int
    return: c * 10 + a
end: tst
int: code 7
if: tst(zz: 5) != 35
    code: 81
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
